From 8538d2ae3086bf187a0b6a2bdf83baabcbd667a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alp Lab AB <dev@alplab.ai>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:44:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] alif devkit_e7: S80KS5122 HyperRAM init for OSPI0 (UNTESTED
 ON SILICON)

Add an opt-in driver (S80K_HYPERRAM_EN=1) that brings up the Infineon/
Cypress S80KS5122 512 Mbit dual-die HyperRAM on OSPI0 and arms its XIP
window, for the Alp Lab E1M-AEN803. Alif's TF-A has no init for this part
(alp-sdk#1970).

The register sequence is transcribed step for step from the Alif Ensemble
CMSIS DFP -- ospi_psram_xip.c ospi_psram_xip_init() plus the device hook in
S80K_HyperRAM.c -- with every write citing its DFP file:line. CR0, wait
cycles and the second die follow the S80KS5122 datasheet where the DFP's
single-die RTSS values would be wrong for this part.

UNTESTED ON SILICON: the only board carrying the part (E1M-AEN803
2626-r2) has CK/CK# crossed at the device, so the driver is gated by
S80K_HYPERRAM_CLK_PAIR_CROSSED (default 1), which makes it log and leave
the device untouched. Build with =0 for a corrected board.

Off by default; an unset build differs from stock only in the build
timestamp.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Alp Lab AB
---
